.serena/

# The empirical evaluation lives on the `eval-phase1` branch, in its own
# worktree at ../doc-standard-eval, and is deliberately never merged here: this
# repo is public and eval/pilot/ contains internal data from a private repo used
# as one of the test corpora. See eval/PLAN.md ("Publication constraint") there.
#
# The worktree is why it is checked out separately rather than switched between:
# the eval tree carries ~28k untracked files (a venv, the agentbench clone,
# caches) that no branch tracks, so `git checkout main` cannot remove them and
# they would sit in this checkout looking like uncommitted work. This entry is a
# backstop in case the two ever share a directory again; it only affects `main`,
# since an ignore rule cannot hide files git already tracks.
eval/